# Security Alerts (ticket 16).
# Needs a Tenant Admin access token with an Active Tenant (see http/tenants.http). To see each rule
# fire, you also need another member (http/invitations.http) and an enabled Application with its
# client credentials (http/access-checks.http).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:9800
@tenantToken = paste-tenant-admin-access-token
@memberEmail = paste-a-members-email
@membershipId = paste-that-members-membership-id
@clientId = paste-client-id
@clientSecret = paste-client-secret
@alertId = paste-alert-id

### -------------------------------------------------------------- Raising alerts

### Rule: Tenant Admin flag changed. Giving the flag raises an alert (granted: true)...
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/memberships/{{membershipId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isTenantAdmin": true }

### ...and so does removing it (granted: false). Both name the member and who changed it.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/memberships/{{membershipId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isTenantAdmin": false }

### Rule: repeated failed logins. Send this 5 times within 15 minutes: the 5th raises one alert in
### every Tenant the member belongs to; more failures in the window raise nothing more. (It also
### locks the account for 15 minutes.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{memberEmail}}", "password": "wrong-password" }

### Rule: refresh-token reuse. After the member has chosen this Tenant, refresh once with their
### sentinel_refresh cookie, then send the same (now used) cookie again: 401, the login is ended
### everywhere, and an alert is raised in this Tenant.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/refresh
Cookie: sentinel_refresh=paste-an-already-used-refresh-token

### Rule: denied Access Checks. With no Role in the Application this is denied; send it 50 times
### within 5 minutes (a loop with curl is easier) for one alert. More denials in the next 5 minutes
### raise nothing more.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/access-checks
Authorization: Basic {{clientId}}:{{clientSecret}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "accessToken": "{{tenantToken}}", "action": "read", "resourceType": "Invoice" }

### -------------------------------------------------------------- Tenant Admin: alerts

### Open alerts, newest first. Each has rule, status, subject (the User it is about), actor (who
### changed the flag), application (for denied Access Checks), details and acknowledgement.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/security-alerts?status=open
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Filter by rule: repeated-failed-logins, refresh-token-reused, access-check-denials-spike,
### tenant-admin-changed. Paginated with limit and cursor.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/security-alerts?rule=tenant-admin-changed&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Acknowledge one. Any Tenant Admin can; writes security_alert.acknowledged.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/security-alerts/{{alertId}}/acknowledge
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### 409: already acknowledged
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/security-alerts/{{alertId}}/acknowledge
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Acknowledged ones
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/security-alerts?status=acknowledged
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### 400: unknown rule
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/security-alerts?rule=nope
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
